<section class="setup">
    <h2>🛠️ Lab Setup: Simulating Internet Access with NAT</h2>
    <p class="intro-text">
        This setup will guide you through connecting a Virtual PC to a NAT node to simulate internet access in <strong>GNS3</strong>. Make sure your NAT device is available in the device list.
    </p>

    <div class="setup-step">
        <div class="step-header">
            <span class="step-number">1</span>
            <h3>Launch GNS3 and Create a New Project</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
            <div class="instruction-card">
                <div class="instruction-icon">💻</div>
                <div class="instruction-text">
                    Open <strong>GNS3</strong> and start a new project (e.g., <span class="highlight">ILab1</span>)
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="visual-guide">
                <p><strong>Add these devices:</strong></p>
                <div class="device-grid">
                    <div class="device-item">
                        <div class="device-icon">☁️</div>
                        <div>1 NAT Node</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="device-item">
                        <div class="device-icon">🖥️</div>
                        <div>1 VPCS</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="connection-guide">
                <p><strong>Make these connections:</strong></p>
                <div class="connection-visual">
                    <div class="connection-line">
                        <span>VPCS</span> <span class="arrow">→</span> <span>NAT</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
        <div class="step-header">
            <span class="step-number">2</span>
            <h3>Configure the Virtual PC (VPCS)</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
            <div class="instruction-card important">
                <div class="instruction-icon">⌨️</div>
                <div class="instruction-text">
                    Access the VPCS console by right-clicking and selecting <span class="highlight">Console</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="config-section">
                <div class="device-config full-width">
                    <h4>Assign IP Address and Gateway</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">Enter these commands:</div>
                        <code>ip 192.168.122.10 255.255.255.0 192.168.122.1</code>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="verification">
                <p>Verify your configuration:</p>
                <div class="code-block">
                    <code>show</code>
                </div>
                <div class="expected-output">
                    <p><strong>Expected Output:</strong></p>
                    <pre>NAME   IP/MASK              GATEWAY           MAC                DNS
VPCS1  192.168.122.10/24  192.168.122.1     00:50:79:66:68:00</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
        <div class="step-header">
            <span class="step-number">3</span>
            <h3>Test Internet Access</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
            <div class="test-instructions">
                <h4>Testing Your NAT Configuration</h4>

                <div class="test-case">
                    <div class="test-number">1</div>
                    <div class="test-content">
                        <p><strong>Basic connectivity test:</strong></p>
                        <div class="code-block">
                            <code>ping 192.168.122.1</code> <span class="comment"># Ping the NAT gateway (should work)</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="test-case">
                    <div class="test-number">2</div>
                    <div class="test-content">
                        <p><strong>Internet simulation test:</strong></p>
                        <div class="code-block">
                            <code>ping 8.8.8.8</code> <span class="comment"># Ping Google's DNS (should work if NAT is functioning)</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="test-case">
                    <div class="test-number">3</div>
                    <div class="test-content">
                        <p><strong>Path verification:</strong></p>
                        <div class="code-block">
                            <code>trace 8.8.8.8</code> <span class="comment"># View the path to the destination</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="note-box tip">
                <div class="note-icon">🔍</div>
                <div class="note-text">
                    <strong>NAT Insight:</strong> The NAT device translates your private IP (192.168.122.10) to a public IP when communicating with external networks, simulating real internet access.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="completion-message success">
        <h3>🎉 NAT Configuration Successful!</h3>
        <p>You've successfully configured NAT to simulate internet access in GNS3!</p>
        <div class="next-steps">
            <p><strong>Challenge:</strong> Try adding a second VPCS and test communication between them through the NAT.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

